<div class="wrap narrow">
  <header class="page-head"><h1>About</h1></header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>enihongo is a free website for learning Japanese. Short lessons you can follow on a phone, in Vietnamese or English.</p>
    <h2>Our goal</h2>
    <p>To help beginners start Japanese gently: read the letters, build a solid foundation, then move step by step towards conversation and the basic exams. Each lesson takes about 10 minutes, so it is easy to keep up every day.</p>
    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Complete beginners who do not know any letters yet.</li>
      <li>People preparing to study or work in Japan who need a solid base.</li>
      <li>Learners who want to review the alphabets and basic vocabulary.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Our promise</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Free, no ads and no account needed.</li>
      <li>All content is written by the project.</li>
      <li>Your progress stays on your own device.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Roadmap</h2>
    <p>Available: Hiragana and Katakana.</p>
    <p>Coming next: elementary Japanese, basic kanji, conversation, listening.</p>
    <p>Send feedback and bug reports through <a href="{{ site.repo }}">GitHub</a>.</p>
    <p class="hint">Stroke order data: KanjiVG by Ulrich Apel, licensed CC BY-SA 3.0.</p>
  </div>
</div>
